erstanding social behavior during  crisis they allow us to test theories in  in ways we just really couldn't do in  the past okay so we have to refined and  extend our theories but there's really  interesting things to be learned so this  this research agenda isn't cheap right  what is it entail it means we have to  make use of qualitative methods  statistical and machine learning methods  text analysis network analysis right all  kinds of different methods and it means  we have to incorporate data from a lot  of different sources right not just  social media data but census data  interview data all kinds of different  things and this is sort of multi-method  multi-modal approach is I think what  computational social science has to  offer to help improve our understanding  of social behavior during crisis events  all right so this is a large project let  me just quickly thank my collaborators  right I have a number of awesome  colleagues who helped with this work we  have a team of student researchers who  also participate in these projects and  of course we couldn't do it without our  funders so thank you  you
 

